5.2.1 Bamboo scaffolds, metal scaffolds and truss-out bamboo scaffolds are widely used in the maintenance works of buildings/structures as well as other work-at-height. The general safety requirements are as follows:
i. The scaffold should be so properly designed, constructed and maintained and every part thereof kept so securely supported or suspended so as to ensure that the scaffold is stable;
ii. Scaffolding members shall be of sound materials, good construction, adequate strength and free from patent defects and should be properly maintained;
iii. The working platform on the scaffold should be provided with suitable and safe
access and egress, closely boarded and provided with the safety installations listed in Annex;
iv. Catch-fans and protective screens should be provided (except for truss-out bamboo scaffolds);
v. No scaffold should be erected, substantially added to, altered or dismantled except by trained workmen with adequate experience and under the immediate supervision of a competent person. The competent person should carry out supervisory work under safe circumstances and focus on monitoring the safety condition of the scaffold and the safety of the trained workmen. The competent person should not engage in the scaffolding work. No workman shall make unauthorised alteration to the scaffold or work on an unfinished scaffold;

